Ha, I did it!

First, a bit of me and Nethack: I learned that it exists from the
internet game Kingdom of Loathing (witch has a whole Nethack area). In
early February this year I decided that I'm gonna give it a try. I'd
never believe I can ascend that soon, after all, my best so far was
Valley of the Dead and then a few deaths in Fort Ludios. Thatswhy I
didn't keep many notes, so no extensive descriptions here. Also, I have
yet to find something that will save the epilogue to a text file..

Anyway, the start was not bad, not great either - found a lamp on level
4 and rubbed it - a magic one that was and a djinni was summoned,
unfortunately with hostile thoughts. Luckily he was survivable..
Gnomish mines first, the town had nothing worth mentioning. Desdended
deeper, where I stepped on a poly trap and became a Yellow Dragon - a
little dragon army followed soon. Kept one and ditched the rest in the
bottom level. The (counter-aligned) priest managed to die somehow by
the little dragon's claw, so no protection for me (I shoul've bought
some with a lower level anyway).

Sokoban's next, all went smoothly until I started to return with the
bag of holding back to normal dungeon - the dragon was untamed. Bah.
Found a neutral altar in the 11th or so level, sacrificed a bit to get
Mjollnir, it worked like a charm with the glowes of power from a shop.
Proceeded further, a big room appeared, only the second time I've seen
it (and the first time I survived :) Got lucky and found a portal to
the Fort, where I died a few times before, but what the hell. Cleared
the zoo and all the soldiers, two black dragons guarding the castle
destroyed my shield, cloak (enchanted one from a throne) and armor -
yikes. Retreat!

Another magic lamp was used after I ate a tengu and got jumpy - wished
for a =oTC, only to find out that I had one unided.. Decided to do the
quest next - it wasn't that hard (first time done it) and the Orb of
Fate was mine. Descended further, found an altar with a priest of Odin.
Before I could improve my AC he got killed by my zruty (ex-dog + poly
wand, I kept it because its description says it's from the Tatra
mountains - thatswhere I'm from. Never heard about a zruty though..), a
bit of sacrificing and I got crowned. Next level was Medusa with the
island in the middle, piece of cake. With a shield of reflection I
returned to the Fort and cleared it. Made some dragon scale mail for
the first time, now I can wish for them too!

Castle was pretty easy, had to smash the bridge and freeze water
though, forgot an instrument. A WoW, hooray, improved my equipment to
the standart - had helm of telepathy, GDSM (self-made), gauntlets of
power, boots of speed, all nicely enchanted. Do you notice the lack of
a cloak? I did too, after I cleared the whole Gehennom... Donated some
75k to the priest of Moloch to get at least some protection, my AC was
37 or so. Good enough.

Speaking of Gehennom, the mazes frustrated me because I did not have a
good way to map them - all my scrolls and potions got cleared in the
swampy room where I fell into water (had magic breathing from an amulet
luckily). D'oh. I forgot to take out some cash and had to kill those
demons - pretty easy. Desdended further, found the vibrating square,
then found Vlad's tower and killed him. Same with Rodney, who appeared
at the sanctum just when I was fighting the High priest,
double-troubled me and stole my Orb of Fate, Geryon was summoned too.
Ouch. That was probably the only part in the game when my HP dropped
below the half (had about 300 at the time).

Back to level 1 without many problems, although the Wizard kept
respawning, for a total of 10 times. Still piece of cake :P All planes
but Air were easy, some bastard (Titan or Archon) summoned lots of
monsters and I had to teleport them away and retreat above. Now the
final location. Lots and lots of monsters there, killed Famine eleven
times, Pestilience five an Death twice until I was sure where to
sacrifice the amulet. And done :)

I learned lots of things this run - don't play 12 hours straight,
protect your scrolls and potions, get lots of holy water (I had nearly
everything cursed from Rodney), and.. it is doable. Yay! Now for a
different class.. :)



